# 💻 Adapter: .cursorrules (L1)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **[PRIME DIRECTIVE]**: You are operating under the AI Context OS. Your VERY FIRST action in a new session MUST be to silently **READ** the file `.ai-context-os/.ultp_state` to synchronize environment state. DO NOT execute shell commands for boot.
> **[MEMORY]**: Read `.ai-context-os/memory/session.md` (if exists) to establish continuity from previous agents.
> **Law:** Read and adhere to the entire AI Operating System at: `.ai-context-os/PROJECT_OS.md`.
> **Localization:** Reply to the user in their initial prompt language (e.g., Vietnamese).

## Cursor-Specific Capabilities
- **File Referencing:** Use `@` mentions when reading or modifying files to ensure maximum context accuracy.
- **Code Generation:** Do not explain obvious things. Output only the necessary code changes.
- **Indexing:** Rely on Cursor's fast codebase indexing. Do not blindly `grep` or `find` if you can use semantic search.

Default AI adapter reference: `.ai-context-os/.cursorrules`

## ⚠️ PTY Compatibility — CRITICAL for terminal commands

> [!CAUTION]
> When running commands via Cursor's terminal, child processes can inherit PTY file
> descriptors and prevent command completion detection. The agent will hang
> waiting for a "done" status that never arrives.

**ALWAYS append `</dev/null` to these commands:**

| Command | Why |
|---------|-----|
| `git commit`, `git push`, `git pull` | GPG agent holds PTY |
| `docker compose up/down/exec/build` | Docker CLI spawns children |
| Any script with `&` (background jobs) | Background process inherits PTY |

```bash
# ✅ Correct
git commit --no-verify -m "message" </dev/null
docker compose down </dev/null
./run-tests.sh --api --smoke </dev/null

# ❌ Wrong — will cause hang
git commit -m "message"
docker compose down
```

## 🧪 Testing — MANDATORY RULES

> [!WARNING]
> **NEVER run `cargo test`, `npm test`, `npx playwright test`, or any test
> command directly.** This project uses Docker-based test isolation.
> The ONLY way to run tests is through `./run-tests.sh`.

| What you want | Command |
|---------------|---------|
| Quick lint + unit | `./run-tests.sh --api --smoke </dev/null` |
| Full test suite | `./run-tests.sh --all </dev/null` |
| Single test | `./run-tests.sh --api --test-only --test=test_name </dev/null` |

**After fixing code, ALWAYS verify with `./run-tests.sh` before claiming done.**
